; The partner's leads. Winning 42 p. 5 (S-0018-b) and pp. 37-40 (S-0057-b, S-0059-a,
; S-0059-b, S-0059-c, S-0060-b, S-0060-c); played in Hands 15, 29, 30 and 31
; (S-0049-b, S-0134-a, S-0135-e, S-0135-h, S-0139-d, S-0139-e).
; Rule, in our words: the bidder's partner on lead leads, in order: a double
; or the top unplayed tile of a suit (a walker, as good as a double); else a
; tile that calls for no count (its suit's count is played, in his own hand,
; or trump); else one that calls for only a five; else a six, which calls for
; only a ten, before a four or a five, which can call for both. He never leads
; trump.
; Replaces gates/c09-partner-never-leads-trump.silas and
; gates/c23-partner-leads-doubles.silas. How it differs: the gates lead
; doubles only, and step aside for a walker without leading it (S-0059-c: the
; 4-3 once the 4-4, 4-5 and 4-6 are gone); the book ranks the walker with the
; doubles (S-0060-b). The book's one exception to "never trump" (S-0060-c) is
; narrower than the gate header's: every other lead is a four, five or six
; calling big count, and even then a six goes first unless the partner is
; fairly sure the bidder holds more than one trump.
; GAP likelihood: that exception reads the bidder's trumps from his bid and
; play, a belief over his hand; it is not encoded, so trump is never led.

(include book)

(policy partner-leads
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-a-double-or-the-top-tile
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair p) (domino lead))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (bidders-partner p)
          (on-lead p)
          (own-legal lead)
          (walker lead)))))
  (rule lead-what-calls-no-count
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair p) (domino lead))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (bidders-partner p)
          (on-lead p)
          (own-legal lead)
          (not (trump-tile lead))
          (not (calls-for-count lead))))))
  (rule lead-what-calls-only-a-five
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair p) (domino lead))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (bidders-partner p)
          (on-lead p)
          (own-legal lead)
          (not (trump-tile lead))
          (not (calls-for lead 10))))))
  (rule lead-what-calls-only-a-ten
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair p) (domino lead))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (bidders-partner p)
          (on-lead p)
          (own-legal lead)
          (not (trump-tile lead))
          (not (calls-for lead 5))))))
  (rule never-trump
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair p) (domino lead))
        (out lead)
        (pattern
          (viewer p)
          (bidders-partner p)
          (on-lead p)
          (own-legal lead)
          (not (trump-tile lead)))))))
